{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## What happens\n\nWhen `gerrit_safe_submit.py` receives HTTP 409 from the revision-scoped submit\nendpoint, it reports the refusal without the response body Gerrit returned. The body\ncarries the reason — a merge conflict, an unsatisfied submit requirement, a\nRebase-If-Necessary failure, or a genuinely newer patch set — and those demand\ndifferent responses from the caller.\n\nReproduced on current `main` (73e90b296e2) by driving `main()` against a local HTTP\nserver that answers the submit POST with 409 and the plain-text body\n`Cannot rebase db3f3e396f1: Change 3169 could not be rebased due to a conflict during merge. ... * docs/release-notes.md`:\nthe script exits 2 and stderr is exactly\n`refusing stale submit: Gerrit reports revision is no longer current` — the body is absent.\nThe same harness answering 500 with body `internal boom detail` raises\n`HTTPError: HTTP Error 500` with nothing on stderr, so the body is lost on non-409\nfailures too.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n409 is the one status where the correct next action is not inferable from the status\nalone. Without the body the caller has to open the change in a browser to learn\nwhether to rebase, wait for a vote, or resolve a conflict. In an agent session that is\na dead end, because the body is the only place the distinction exists.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe submit POST is wrapped at `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` `main()` in\n`except urllib.error.HTTPError as exc:`, which prints a fixed line for 409 and\nre-raises everything else without calling `exc.read()`. `urllib.error.HTTPError` is a\nfile-like response, so the body is available from `exc.read()` at that point. When it is\nconstructed with `fp=None` (as the existing tests at\n`tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py` do for their 409 and 500 stubs),\n`HTTPError.__init__` substitutes `io.BytesIO()`, so `read()` returns `b''` rather than\nraising. Measured: `urllib.error.HTTPError('u', 409, 'c', {}, None).read()` returns `b''`\non CPython 3.11.16, 3.12.14, 3.13.17 and 3.14.9, which covers every interpreter in CI's\n`python-version: [\"3.11\", \"3.12\", \"3.13\"]` matrix. The existing stubs therefore exercise\nthe empty-body path, not an exception path.\n\n1. Add one helper, `_error_body(exc)`, that reads `exc.read()`, decodes it as UTF-8\n   with `errors=\"replace\"`, and strips the `)]}'` XSSI prefix with the existing\n   `_strip_xssi`. If the remainder parses as a JSON object with a string `message`\n   field, return that message; otherwise return the stripped text unchanged (non-JSON\n   is never an error). A read that raises `OSError` yields an empty string.\n2. In the 409 branch, keep today's line verbatim and print a second line\n   `Gerrit response (HTTP 409): <body>`, then return 2 exactly as today.\n3. In the non-409 branch, print `Gerrit response (HTTP <code>): <body>` to stderr and\n   then re-raise as today, so the traceback and exit status are unchanged and the\n   output is a superset.\n\nNo new configuration, dependency, or module; the change stays inside\n`scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `scripts/gerrit_safe_submit.py` — the helper and the two print sites above.\n- `tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py` — new regression tests next to\n  the existing `test_safe_submit_returns_stale_when_submit_races_to_409` and\n  `test_safe_submit_reraises_non_409_submit_http_error`.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests drive `main()` with `_credential` and `_request` monkeypatched (no network),\nraising `urllib.error.HTTPError(path, code, msg, {}, io.BytesIO(body))` from the submit\nPOST:\n\n- 409 with JSON body `{\"message\": \"revision abc is not current revision\"}` → stderr\n  contains `revision abc is not current revision` and `409`; exit 2.\n- 409 with body `)]}'\\n{\"message\": \"x\"}` → stderr contains `x` and not `)]}'`.\n- 409 with plain-text merge-conflict body (the 3169 text above) → stderr contains\n  `docs/release-notes.md`; no exception.\n- 409 with an empty body → exit 2, today's line still printed.\n- 409 with a JSON body that has no string `message`, `{\"status\": \"CONFLICT\"}` → stderr\n  contains the literal text `{\"status\": \"CONFLICT\"}`; no exception.\n- 500 with body `internal boom detail` → `HTTPError` still raised with code 500 and\n  stderr contains `internal boom detail` and `500`.\n\nThe existing tests in that file must keep passing unchanged, which pins the unchanged\nguard behaviour (which revisions are accepted) and the unchanged 409 exit code.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] **AC1** On a stubbed 409 whose body carries a `message` field, the script's\n      stderr contains that message text verbatim.\n- [x] **AC2** The stderr also still contains the HTTP status code, so the output is a\n      superset of today's.\n- [x] **AC3** A body prefixed with `)]}'` is printed with that prefix removed.\n- [x] **AC4** A body that is not a JSON object with a string `message` field (plain\n      text, or JSON such as `{\"status\": \"CONFLICT\"}`) is printed as-is rather than raising.\n- [x] **AC5** The exit code on 409 is unchanged from today's (2).\n- [x] **AC6** Unit tests covering AC1-AC5 against stubbed responses, with no network\n      access, pass under `pytest tests/unit/test_gerrit_submit_if_current_8b1c.py`.\n- [x] **AC7** `make lint` exits 0 locally.\n- [x] **AC8** `make typecheck` exits 0 locally.\n- [x] **AC9** The Gerrit change carries `Verified +1`; CI's gating cell runs the same\n      `not integration and not external` selection as `make verify`'s test step.\n\n## Out of scope\n\nThe abbreviated-SHA guard defect in the same script, tracked separately on\n`triumphant-dated-kingsnake`. This change\nmust not alter which revisions the guard accepts. Rewording the 409 message itself (it\nstill says \"no longer current\") is tracked separately on\n`tenuous-decorative-chimpanzee`; this change only adds the body."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793472948002749001,"uuid":"95f08d5c-c3c2-49cc-9fcb-58ff88499520"}